[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability lies in the use of a cryptographic hash function without specifying a salt. When hashing sensitive data like certificates, failing to use a salt means that identical inputs will produce identical hash outputs. This predictability can be exploited by attackers using precomputed rainbow tables to quickly determine the original input (the certificate) from its hash, thereby compromising the security of the hashed data.

